WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.050 --> 00:00:06.420
We're back in the 90s for the first awesome
Captain Marvel trailer and boy does it look

00:00:06.420 --> 00:00:07.420
fantastic!

00:00:07.420 --> 00:00:11.640
Yippee-ki-yay, movie lovers, it's Jan here
and in this video I'm breaking down the trailer

00:00:11.640 --> 00:00:15.880
for loads of marvellous easter eggs and crucial
details you might have missed.

00:00:15.880 --> 00:00:19.859
And to celebrate the Captain Marvel trailer,
I'm kicking off a new superhero giveaway,

00:00:19.859 --> 00:00:23.810
so make sure you're subscribed to my channel
and leave me comment below on the trailer

00:00:23.810 --> 00:00:25.570
for a chance to win!

00:00:25.570 --> 00:00:29.630
The first detail you might have missed comes
in this brief shot in a lab deep inside a

00:00:29.630 --> 00:00:30.909
SHIELD building.

00:00:30.909 --> 00:00:35.220
If you zoom in really close, you'll see Nick
Fury with a gun presumably ready in case the

00:00:35.220 --> 00:00:37.850
Skrull on the operating table wakes up.

00:00:37.850 --> 00:00:42.809
And notice how Fury is holding what looks
like some kind of cold pack on his left eye.

00:00:42.809 --> 00:00:46.730
Now, obviously, elsewhere in the trailer we
see a younger Fury before the injury that

00:00:46.730 --> 00:00:49.629
led him to wear an eyepatch in the other MCU
movies.

00:00:49.629 --> 00:00:53.980
So, I think that what we're seeing in this
scene is the aftermath of a fight with a Skrull

00:00:53.980 --> 00:00:59.070
which caused Fury's left eye injury and led
him to have to wear an eye patch.

00:00:59.070 --> 00:01:03.559
Also facing away from us is someone else who
looks to me like it could be Ben Mendelsohn.

00:01:03.559 --> 00:01:08.250
You might know him as Krennic from Rogue One,
but in Captain Marvel he's playing the alien

00:01:08.250 --> 00:01:13.220
Skrull, Talos, who arrives on earth and shape-shifts
into human form to hide among us in plain

00:01:13.220 --> 00:01:14.220
sight.

00:01:14.220 --> 00:01:18.180
Talos is the leader of the Skrulls who have
been at war with the alien Kree race and he

00:01:18.180 --> 00:01:23.400
arrives on Earth to pose as a SHIELD agent
and secretly lay the groundwork for a Skrull

00:01:23.400 --> 00:01:24.400
invasion.

00:01:24.400 --> 00:01:28.700
And this scene gives us a glimpse of how perfectly
he seems to be blending in!

00:01:28.700 --> 00:01:33.200
And as that shot of Talos and Nick Fury appears,
the trailer drops the following voiceover

00:01:33.200 --> 00:01:36.270
line from Samuel L. Jackson: "space invasion".

00:01:36.270 --> 00:01:40.590
Now that's another subtle indication that
Captain Marvel is drawing from the "Secret

00:01:40.590 --> 00:01:42.970
Invasion" comic-book crossover storyline.

00:01:42.970 --> 00:01:47.490
In that story, it's revealed that the shape-shifting
Skrulls have actually taken the place of many

00:01:47.490 --> 00:01:52.280
of Marvel's superheroes, so it'll be interesting
to see if the Captain Marvel movie gives any

00:01:52.280 --> 00:01:58.170
hints as to whether any of our favourite MCU
characters are actually secret Skrull imposters!

00:01:58.170 --> 00:02:03.210
And that shocking shot of Captain Marvel thumping
what seems to be a poor old lady on the train

00:02:03.210 --> 00:02:06.220
might have confused you if you weren't familiar
with the Skrulls.

00:02:06.220 --> 00:02:11.030
But I suspect Carol's seen whoever she was
chasing on top of the train shape-shift into

00:02:11.030 --> 00:02:15.880
a human form, or it could be that something
in the way the old lady smiles at Carol triggers

00:02:15.880 --> 00:02:20.870
a memory or a reaction from her Kree background,
making her think this woman's a Skrull.

00:02:20.870 --> 00:02:24.605
I wonder whether the real twist will be that
she's really is just an old lady and the attack

00:02:24.605 --> 00:02:25.605
might put Carol on the authorities' radar
which could be how she eventually ends up

00:02:25.605 --> 00:02:26.605
at SHIELD and meeting Nick Fury.

00:02:26.605 --> 00:02:27.605
"So you're not from around here?"

00:02:27.605 --> 00:02:28.605
"It's hard to explain"
The trailer also teases some cool new details

00:02:28.605 --> 00:02:32.700
about Captain Marvel's origins which as Carol
Danvers says are definitely complicated.

00:02:32.700 --> 00:02:37.280
Marvel's confirmed this won't be your typical
superhero origin story as the movie will begin

00:02:37.280 --> 00:02:42.700
with Carol Danvers already having her powers
and she'll be part of a Kree elite unit called

00:02:42.700 --> 00:02:43.700
Starforce.

00:02:43.700 --> 00:02:47.030
The trailer teases a few shots of her fellow
Kree teammates.

00:02:47.030 --> 00:02:51.890
On the right of Carol Danvers in the Starforce
shot is Minn-Erva, played by Gemma Chan.

00:02:51.890 --> 00:02:56.260
Minn-Erva is an elite sniper and was the star
of the team before Carol joined, so you can

00:02:56.260 --> 00:02:59.100
expect some rivalry between them in the movie.

00:02:59.100 --> 00:03:02.690
There's Korath there, who you'll have seen
in Guardians of the Galaxy as the Kree mercenary

00:03:02.690 --> 00:03:06.680
who'd been sent by Thanos to retrieve the
Orb which contained the Power Stone.

00:03:06.680 --> 00:03:10.430
Because we're going back in time this will
be a younger Korath, though he's still played

00:03:10.430 --> 00:03:11.790
by the same actor.

00:03:11.790 --> 00:03:16.020
I suspect that the Captain Marvel movie will
show us why he and Ronan ended up allying

00:03:16.020 --> 00:03:19.520
themselves with Thanos by the time of the
Guardians of the Galaxy movie.

00:03:19.520 --> 00:03:23.490
By the way, Ronan appears very briefly in
the trailer with his back to us in this shot

00:03:23.490 --> 00:03:24.490
here.

00:03:24.490 --> 00:03:29.780
In charge of the team is Jude Law whose character
I think could be responsible for wiping Carol's

00:03:29.780 --> 00:03:30.780
memories.

00:03:30.780 --> 00:03:32.740
"I keep having these memories."

00:03:32.740 --> 00:03:35.170
"I see flashes."

00:03:35.170 --> 00:03:36.540
"I think I had a life here."

00:03:36.540 --> 00:03:41.170
"But I can't tell if it's real."

00:03:41.170 --> 00:03:45.790
The assumption so far with Law's character
is that he's playing Mar-vell, however, nobody's

00:03:45.790 --> 00:03:50.840
been able to confirm who his character actually
is, meaning it could be part of a twist.

00:03:50.840 --> 00:03:52.000
Let me know what you think.

00:03:52.000 --> 00:03:57.160
OK, so this is a scene of an experiment or
procedure that I suspect Jude Law's character

00:03:57.160 --> 00:03:59.140
may be performing on Carol.

00:03:59.140 --> 00:04:03.610
Interviews with Brie Larson and Kevin Feige
have confirmed Captain Marvel is part-human,

00:04:03.610 --> 00:04:07.900
part-Kree in the movie, as in the comics,
and let's just say this scene feels like she's

00:04:07.900 --> 00:04:10.680
being turned into a Kree Winter Soldier.

00:04:10.680 --> 00:04:14.810
This could be a twist on how she receives
her powers in the comics where she was caught

00:04:14.810 --> 00:04:19.819
in a special piece of Kree technology that
altered her DNA making her a human-Kree hybrid

00:04:19.819 --> 00:04:21.359
with superhuman powers.

00:04:21.359 --> 00:04:26.189
Based on the trailer, there is another possibility
for how Carol gets her powers and that's when

00:04:26.189 --> 00:04:30.840
she approaches some wreckage and seems to
be enveloped in a wave of blue light.

00:04:30.840 --> 00:04:34.599
This might also match with another shot in
the trailer where she falls back and then

00:04:34.599 --> 00:04:36.840
you see blue light around her hand.

00:04:36.840 --> 00:04:41.639
An earlier version of the beeper that we saw
in the Avengers: Infinity War post-credits

00:04:41.639 --> 00:04:43.569
scene makes an appearance in the trailer.

00:04:43.569 --> 00:04:47.710
Although it's different, the buttons which
are visible do seem to the match the device

00:04:47.710 --> 00:04:49.270
used in Infinity War.

00:04:49.270 --> 00:04:53.629
The later version appears to be an enhanced
or augmented model with additional attachments

00:04:53.629 --> 00:04:54.629
to the top and bottom.

00:04:54.629 --> 00:04:59.909
The Infinity War model has also aged significantly
and the extra pieces may be necessary to be

00:04:59.909 --> 00:05:04.150
able to communicate with Captain Marvel wherever
she's located at the time of Thanos acquiring

00:05:04.150 --> 00:05:06.029
the Infinity Gauntlet.

00:05:06.029 --> 00:05:10.680
There's also some really interesting foreshadowing
for Avengers 4 in this bit of voiceover from

00:05:10.680 --> 00:05:11.870
Nick Fury:
"We have no idea what threats are out there."

00:05:11.870 --> 00:05:15.069
"We can't do this alone.

00:05:15.069 --> 00:05:16.810
We need you."

00:05:16.810 --> 00:05:20.800
I think we'll hear that line towards the end
of this film, perhaps as Captain Marvel's

00:05:20.800 --> 00:05:22.830
having to leave Earth for some reason.

00:05:22.830 --> 00:05:27.210
Nick Fury will probably be letting Carol know
that he may need to use the beeper to contact

00:05:27.210 --> 00:05:31.270
her again in the case of an emergency, which
is, of course, exactly what happens at the

00:05:31.270 --> 00:05:32.870
end of Infinity War.

00:05:32.870 --> 00:05:35.520
There's also an intriguing line at the end
of the trailer:

00:05:35.520 --> 00:05:36.930
"I'm not who you think I am."

00:05:36.930 --> 00:05:39.509
Notice there's a head just at the bottom of
the frame.

00:05:39.509 --> 00:05:44.819
I think that could be Monica Rambeau the daughter
of Maria Rambeau who's Carol's air force colleague

00:05:44.819 --> 00:05:47.430
and friend who we see earlier in the trailer.

00:05:47.430 --> 00:05:52.270
Maria Rambeau, Monica's mother, goes by the
call sign "Photon" and in the comics, her

00:05:52.270 --> 00:05:56.330
daughter Monica is actually the first female
Captain Marvel.

00:05:56.330 --> 00:06:00.710
This is an interesting easter eggy twist of
sorts and probably a wink by Marvel to comic

00:06:00.710 --> 00:06:05.479
book fans, but what I think is happening in
this scene is that either Carol is revealing

00:06:05.479 --> 00:06:11.029
her superhero alter-ego to her fellow pilot
Maria or perhaps Maria has died and Carol's

00:06:11.029 --> 00:06:15.509
telling her friend's daughter that she's not
the right person to look after her.

00:06:15.509 --> 00:06:19.400
And if that is the young Monica in the bottom
of the shot, then it might be a tease for

00:06:19.400 --> 00:06:23.439
a future super-powered Monica Rambeau in the
MCU.

00:06:23.439 --> 00:06:27.529
Another comic book nod comes with several
shots of Carol Danvers with a helmet.

00:06:27.529 --> 00:06:31.759
And if you look here, you can see the helmet
is being used to create her classic Mohawk

00:06:31.759 --> 00:06:33.599
haircut from the comics.

00:06:33.599 --> 00:06:38.539
And let's just appreciate this amazing final
shot of Captain Marvel fully powering up,

00:06:38.539 --> 00:06:42.039
glowing bright and her eyes turning into pure
light.

00:06:42.039 --> 00:06:46.860
Captain Marvel's powers include the ability
to absorb huge amounts of cosmic energy and

00:06:46.860 --> 00:06:49.039
when she takes on enough she's goes "binary".

00:06:49.039 --> 00:06:53.110
And there's also a cool easter egg on the
Captain Marvel poster as well.

00:06:53.110 --> 00:06:56.770
If you look very carefully, you'll spot the
tail end of a cat here.

00:06:56.770 --> 00:07:01.089
That's a nod to the comics where Carol has
a pet cat called Chewie, named after Chewbacca

00:07:01.089 --> 00:07:02.419
from Star Wars.

00:07:02.419 --> 00:07:07.599
The thing is that Chewie isn't actually a
cat, it's a member of an alien species called

00:07:07.599 --> 00:07:08.919
the Flerken!

00:07:08.919 --> 00:07:13.449
And there was another allusion to the feline-like
alien on some Captain Marvel cupcakes given

00:07:13.449 --> 00:07:16.370
out at an event held at Marvel Studios!

00:07:16.370 --> 00:07:21.099
Notice that cupcake with what look like a
cat's ID tag decoration on it, well that's

00:07:21.099 --> 00:07:26.229
had the internet wondering whether comic-book
Chewie will be renamed in the MCU as Goose!

00:07:26.229 --> 00:07:31.659
That would seem a bit weird given that Disney
own Star Wars, but then again, it would certainly

00:07:31.659 --> 00:07:34.939
fit well with the Top Gun allusions in the
trailers!

00:07:34.939 --> 00:07:40.110
Also on the poster are the words Higher, Further,
Faster, which is a tagline from Captain Marvel's

00:07:40.110 --> 00:07:44.520
comics, specifically a run by writer Kelly
Sue DeConnick whose work has been a particular

00:07:44.520 --> 00:07:45.759
influence on this film.

00:07:45.759 --> 00:07:49.009
So, did the trailer get you hyped for the
Captain Marvel movie?

00:07:49.009 --> 00:07:52.249
And what other details or easter eggs did
you spot?

